course: dictionary
lesson: 944
title: Bloke and British words
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words are used in some countries more than others. A bloke is an informal word for a man, used a lot in Britain, Australia, New Zealand and Ireland. Context helps you work it out: in «a nice bloke», the word nice tells you what kind of man he is.
explain: Check the words around it. «He is a good bloke» means he is a good man. Swap man into the sentence and see if it still makes sense: «He is a good man» does, so bloke means man.
explain: Bloke makes speech sound casual, like friends chatting. Blokey is a related word that means manly and informal, but you will meet bloke far more often.
fact: Bloke means a man, in an informal way.
fact: Bloke is used most in the UK, Australia, New Zealand and Ireland.
fact: In America, people more often say guy for the same idea.
fact: «A bloke is a man.» Swap in man to check your meaning.
fact: «A nice bloke» means a kind, pleasant man.
fact: An ordinary, regular man can be called just a normal bloke.
fact: Blokey means manly and informal.
exercise: «The bloke at the shop helped me find my bag.» What does bloke mean here? | A shop | A bag | *A man | A road sign
exercise: Ellie says, «He's a good bloke.» What does she mean? | *He is a good man | He has a bag of bread | He is a good cook | He is a fast runner
exercise: Which country is bloke most used in? | Egypt | Japan | *Britain | Brazil
test: «He was a nice bloke.» Which word is the best swap for bloke? | bread | road | dog | *man
test: What does blokey mean? | a kind of bread | very hungry | very tall | *manly and informal
exam: Zara from America says guy, and Tom from London says bloke. What do they both mean? | *A man | A car | A town | A joke
